220
00:14:09,693 --> 00:14:12,287
And right now you establish another theme of the film :

221
00:14:12,373 --> 00:14:14,443
" Let 's give her a grandchild and everything will be all right . "

222
00:14:14,533 --> 00:14:16,842
Mary Ann is ready . She 's working . She 's professional .

223
00:14:16,933 --> 00:14:19,731
But she 's ready to start to have a family .

224
00:14:20,093 --> 00:14:24,052
But you hot cut to Kevin Lomax who 's taken the deal . He 's in New York .

225
00:14:25,093 --> 00:14:30,292
At the beginning it 's just a vacation . He 's going to consult on the selection of a jury .

226
00:14:31,213 --> 00:14:35,126
You see Foley Square , the seat of judicial power in New York

227
00:14:36,053 --> 00:14:38,886
all the Federal buildings , the State buildings , the local ...

228
00:14:38,973 --> 00:14:41,203
Everything is right there in one space .

229
00:14:41,293 --> 00:14:46,367
It 's a very , very sobering look at the power of the legal community in New York City .

230
00:14:47,613 --> 00:14:51,367
And at the same time , for a guy from Gainesville , Florida , it 's very impressive .

231
00:14:51,453 --> 00:14:55,241
Kevin 's here . He 's excited . He is working as a consultant

232
00:14:56,093 --> 00:15:00,405
to one of Manhattan 's best and most famous criminal trial attorneys .

233
00:15:01,933 --> 00:15:04,322
His name is Meisel , played by George Wyner .

234
00:15:04,413 --> 00:15:09,123
And in this moment I wanted people to see that Kevin Lomax truly has a talent .

235
00:15:10,173 --> 00:15:13,245
When you talk to criminal attorneys , you realize that they say

236
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:17,645
that between 80 to 95 percent of winning a case is selecting a jury .

237
00:15:18,653 --> 00:15:22,487
This is a scene that I think talks about the inside of lawyering

238
00:15:22,573 --> 00:15:25,007
and the reality of how you win .

239
00:15:25,333 --> 00:15:29,167
You win by psyching-out everyone that 's gonna be on that jury .

240
00:15:29,293 --> 00:15:33,445
Those are the people that are gonna make the decision of whether you win or lose .

241
00:15:33,533 --> 00:15:37,128
This is where Kevin Lomax shines . He has an intuitive spirit .

242
00:15:37,213 --> 00:15:39,727
At the end of the scene , you realize he 's got something else .

243
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,644
He 's got a sixth sense .

244
00:15:41,733 --> 00:15:44,884
Now , it 's important , when we see this courtroom , to understand

245
00:15:44,973 --> 00:15:47,851
that I wanted authenticity in this film . You 're in New York .

246
00:15:47,933 --> 00:15:52,529
You have some of the best looking courtrooms in , I think , the United States .

247
00:15:52,813 --> 00:15:55,805
At the beginning , Warner Bros. Wanted me to go to Canada and shoot in Toronto

248
00:15:55,893 --> 00:15:58,407
which is an entirely different judicial system and the courtrooms

249
00:15:58,493 --> 00:16:01,883
don 't look the same at all . I fought to shoot this film in New York

250
00:16:01,973 --> 00:16:06,091
not only for the fantastic exteriors , but also for these interiors .

251
00:16:06,373 --> 00:16:11,572
This is a film about big-time lawyering , and you want to feel , when you see the sets

252
00:16:13,893 --> 00:16:15,963
and these aren 't sets , they 're locations .

253
00:16:16,053 --> 00:16:18,647
You want to feel that this guy is in the big time .

254
00:16:18,733 --> 00:16:22,408
He 's gone from Gainesville , Florida to the top of the food chain .

255
00:16:22,493 --> 00:16:26,247
We shot in probably seven or eight of the best courtrooms

256
00:16:27,773 --> 00:16:29,604
you could find anywhere in the world .

257
00:16:29,693 --> 00:16:32,685
Look at these paintings up on the wall here in New York .

258
00:16:32,773 --> 00:16:35,571
You feel that this is the justice system .

259
00:16:36,933 --> 00:16:40,562
Now Kevin is exhilarated . He comes out of his first day

260
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:44,009
in the New York courtroom and he knows he 's done well .

261
00:16:44,093 --> 00:16:47,244
He didn 't know how he would measure up , and how he measures up is

262
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:48,561
he 's smarter than they are .

263
00:16:48,653 --> 00:16:51,167
I mean , he has to feel great . He 's walking down the street .

264
00:16:51,253 --> 00:16:54,290
He 's saying I 'm a guy from the hicks , and someone 's watching him .

265
00:16:54,373 --> 00:16:58,491
This is the introduction of John Milton , who 's played by Al Pacino .

266
00:16:58,573 --> 00:17:02,725
It was important to me to establish a very nice introduction to him .

267
00:17:03,133 --> 00:17:05,442
One thing that Al did , and you 'll start to see into this

268
00:17:05,533 --> 00:17:08,127
he chews on licorice all the way through this film .

269
00:17:08,213 --> 00:17:10,681
You don 't explain it . You know he 's doing something .

270
00:17:10,773 --> 00:17:15,403
And instead of just walking away , getting in a limousine , he goes downstairs

271
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:19,372
into the subway . Why would he do that ? He 's well dressed . That 's it .

272
00:17:19,453 --> 00:17:21,967
But immediately I go into a time lapse sequence

273
00:17:22,053 --> 00:17:24,931
and I wanted to see day and night change .

274
00:17:26,853 --> 00:17:29,686
I wanted it to also say that this trial 's been going on for a long time .

275
00:17:29,773 --> 00:17:33,322
When Kevin walks in , Mary Ann says , " You 're home early for a change . "

276
00:17:33,413 --> 00:17:35,847
Time has passed here . You 've seen it pass .

277
00:17:35,933 --> 00:17:39,812
But more importantly , you see Al Pacino going down into the subway

278
00:17:39,893 --> 00:17:43,044
and you see that the next images are not real .

279
00:17:44,293 --> 00:17:47,205
There is a certain kind of power that this person

280
00:17:47,293 --> 00:17:50,091
we don 't even know who he is yet , exudes .

281
00:17:50,173 --> 00:17:53,449
I thought that the time lapse would be both unique in terms of time passage

282
00:17:53,533 --> 00:17:57,811
and , at the same time , extraordinary in terms of the potential power

283
00:17:57,893 --> 00:17:59,531
that this man has .

284
00:17:59,613 --> 00:18:02,252
Now you 've got Wife and Husband in ...

285
00:18:02,853 --> 00:18:05,492
Mary Ann 's got room service all over the room .

286
00:18:05,573 --> 00:18:09,361
Clearly , they 've been there for a long time . She 's watching TV .

287
00:18:09,453 --> 00:18:11,171
She 's having a good time . She 's been shopping .

288
00:18:11,253 --> 00:18:14,404
She 's been to a lot of things , but her husband 's been gone every day .

289
00:18:14,493 --> 00:18:17,769
And now you see the way they play . Kevin looks like he 's defeated .

290
00:18:17,853 --> 00:18:20,492
It looks like he 's lost the case . She feels badly for him .

291
00:18:20,573 --> 00:18:23,690
You can really see how she would , you know , how warm and wonderful

292
00:18:23,773 --> 00:18:26,526
and sweet she is . But he 's kidding her .

293
00:18:26,613 --> 00:18:30,288
You can really see the slyness , I think , in Keanu Reeves here .

294
00:18:30,373 --> 00:18:34,491
And , at the same time , he killed ' em . He actually chose the jury

295
00:18:35,333 --> 00:18:37,449
and won the case , almost an impossible case .

296
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:41,526
It was like a savings-and-Ioan fraud . This is white-collar crime .

297
00:18:42,053 --> 00:18:44,613
The guy sitting there in the trial , with his white hair

298
00:18:44,693 --> 00:18:49,767
looks extremely legit . But the fact is that , you know , he 's like Charles Keating .

299
00:18:50,973 --> 00:18:54,966
You know , he stole not millions , but tens of millions of dollars .

300
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:59,530
And in this instance , the next shot is , they are in John Milton 's domain .

301
00:19:01,733 --> 00:19:06,249
This is Milton , Chadwick and Waters , and I wanted a location that immediately

302
00:19:06,333 --> 00:19:09,370
established the power of this law firm . This is a real building .

303
00:19:09,453 --> 00:19:14,288
It 's the Continental Plaza in Wall Street , in the financial district , Downtown

304
00:19:14,373 --> 00:19:19,367
and you see what New York power is all about . That view is a three-bridge view .

305
00:19:21,093 --> 00:19:23,732
You 're gonna see all the way up the island of Manhattan .

306
00:19:23,813 --> 00:19:28,443
But the important thing here was , this location was used before in other films .

307
00:19:28,533 --> 00:19:32,765
I didn 't want to use that same look . There 's a unique design look here .

308
00:19:32,853 --> 00:19:35,890
Bruno Rubeo , who is my production designer and my collaborator

309
00:19:35,973 --> 00:19:38,407
on the last three films I 've done

310
00:19:38,493 --> 00:19:42,008
we spent probably six to eight months before this film began

311
00:19:42,093 --> 00:19:44,891
talking about what we wanted from this film and the look .

312
00:19:44,973 --> 00:19:48,932
Right now you 're looking at Christabella , the first time we see her

313
00:19:49,013 --> 00:19:53,848
and if you notice as she walks forward , I slowed down . It goes in real time .

314
00:19:54,413 --> 00:19:58,088
There 's no cut there . We ramped so she starts in real time

315
00:19:58,173 --> 00:19:59,242
she slows down

316
00:19:59,333 --> 00:20:00,652
and comes back out in real time .

317
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:04,408
And Kevin Lomax , he doesn 't know why he 's fascinated by her . We 'll find out later .

318
00:20:04,493 --> 00:20:07,690
But look at the design in this . It 's ultra modern .

319
00:20:08,013 --> 00:20:11,642
We used both an Italian architect and a Japanese architect .

320
00:20:11,733 --> 00:20:15,362
This is the Italian . He used prefab concrete in the walls .

321
00:20:17,333 --> 00:20:20,530
Milton 's office . You know , the rest of the building is very impressive

322
00:20:20,613 --> 00:20:22,171
but this office is something else again .

323
00:20:22,253 --> 00:20:25,768
It 's cold , it 's austere , and it 's incredibly impressive .

324
00:20:26,733 --> 00:20:29,486
Look at that fireplace in the background . It 's set up off the floor .

325
00:20:29,573 --> 00:20:32,531
Bruno had a design in mind . The furniture in this place is ...

326
00:20:32,613 --> 00:20:36,208
You have a big , massive place . But look at the furniture .

327
00:20:37,293 --> 00:20:41,411
That little settee in front of the fire : It 's delicate , it 's small .

328
00:20:41,533 --> 00:20:45,367
This whole room exudes taste and a certain stylistic quotient .

329
00:20:45,773 --> 00:20:49,925
John Milton , you know , it 's a huge room , devoid of furniture , very minimal

330
00:20:51,213 --> 00:20:55,206
this is a man who has real taste and real choices that he 's made .

331
00:20:56,413 --> 00:21:00,088
At the same time , this whole law firm is very , very modern .

332
00:21:00,893 --> 00:21:05,091
For the design quotient of this film , I want you to be able to see this sequence

333
00:21:05,173 --> 00:21:07,562
and then later on , when you see where Milton lives , see the dichotomy

334
00:21:07,653 --> 00:21:08,608
the difference .

335
00:21:08,693 --> 00:21:12,368
This is cutting-edge modern architecture to the nth degree .

336
00:21:13,093 --> 00:21:15,971
What Bruno wanted to do , and I wanted to do in this instance

337
00:21:16,053 --> 00:21:18,044
is establish Milton 's environment .

338
00:21:18,133 --> 00:21:22,649
Here it 's cold , corporate , but , at the same time , undeniably impressive

339
00:21:23,293 --> 00:21:25,363
austere , ultra-designed .

340
00:21:27,533 --> 00:21:31,492
Milton is very smooth . You know , Al Pacino always gets this rap :

341
00:21:31,613 --> 00:21:35,811
" Oh , gee , he 's over the top . " He 's not . Al Pacino can play everything .

342
00:21:35,893 --> 00:21:38,043
And everything he did in this film was calculated .

343
00:21:38,133 --> 00:21:42,888
I mean , it was one of the great experiences in my life to work with an actor of

344
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:47,809
his deep , deep ability , his deep , deep talent

345
00:21:48,893 --> 00:21:51,965
and his uncompromising attitude towards all his work .

346
00:21:53,493 --> 00:21:56,724
At the same time , Keanu , who had this ... I 'm saying this because here 's these

347
00:21:56,813 --> 00:21:58,212
two actors meeting for the first time .

348
00:21:58,293 --> 00:22:02,809
Keanu , who had done a lot of young-man roles , a lot of teenage slackers

349
00:22:03,293 --> 00:22:06,808
in this film is anything but that . Kevin Lomax is precise .

350
00:22:06,893 --> 00:22:10,010
He is not a Harvard educated , a Yale educated guy .

351
00:22:11,573 --> 00:22:15,407
He came from a small school in Florida , went to a small law school .

352
00:22:15,493 --> 00:22:18,485
But all criminal attorneys that are really great usually did that .

353
00:22:18,573 --> 00:22:21,804
They come from the street . He 's street smart . He thinks on his feet .

354
00:22:21,893 --> 00:22:26,603
And he 's up against a guy , for the first time , that seems to have a little bit more

355
00:22:26,693 --> 00:22:27,523
on the ball than even he does .

356
00:22:27,613 --> 00:22:30,730
He 's never met anybody before that is his equal .

357
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:33,891
And Milton keeps blowing his mind , like he does right now .

358
00:22:33,973 --> 00:22:37,170
You see this office . All of a sudden , he goes and taps on the door

359
00:22:37,253 --> 00:22:41,166
opens up , and I wanted this sequence to truly be a moment

360
00:22:41,293 --> 00:22:44,569
that would blow everybody 's mind , not only Kevin Lomax 's .

361
00:22:44,653 --> 00:22:48,328
He walks out on a roof terrace and , effectively , I 'm using ...

362
00:22:49,693 --> 00:22:53,402
Again , this is from a Japanese design . Bruno and I saw an architect

363
00:22:53,493 --> 00:22:58,169
that had a pond on the roof in Japan , and I said that is a perfect idea

364
00:22:59,413 --> 00:23:01,131
for what we want to do here .

365
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:04,649
Here is a man who has such a sense of design and such a sense of grandeur

366
00:23:04,733 --> 00:23:09,761
that he has created for himself a balcony , if you will , a terrace , a park on top .

367
00:23:10,453 --> 00:23:15,288
But does it have greenery on it ? No . It has water . He calls it calming , placid .

368
00:23:15,373 --> 00:23:17,887
And at the same time , he 's going to take Keanu out there

369
00:23:17,973 --> 00:23:20,612
and he 's going to talk about his past .

370
00:23:20,773 --> 00:23:24,368
He 's going to find out a little bit more about him . He asks about his father .

371
00:23:24,453 --> 00:23:27,968
Keanu says , " I never had one . " He asks about his mother .

372
00:23:28,173 --> 00:23:32,052
And in this instance he 's , you know , if you look at Al 's reactions here

373
00:23:32,133 --> 00:23:35,364
this is a long , talky sequence . This is what you do sometimes .

374
00:23:35,453 --> 00:23:38,570
By the way , this is real . This is not blue screen .

375
00:23:38,653 --> 00:23:41,292
We didn 't put the artists in a studio .

376
00:23:41,693 --> 00:23:45,242
I fought to get this scene . I fought everyone , including Warner Bros.

377
00:23:45,333 --> 00:23:47,210
Nobody wanted me to go up and get this shot .

378
00:23:47,293 --> 00:23:50,490
It 's on the roof of the Continental Tower . They had re-roofed the place .

379
00:23:50,573 --> 00:23:52,484
The building didn 't want us up there .

380
00:23:52,573 --> 00:23:57,169
I just knew that this sequence was going to define this initial relationship

381
00:23:57,293 --> 00:23:59,602
between Kevin Lomax and John Milton .

382
00:23:59,773 --> 00:24:03,766
And the two actors are basically 50 stories in the air right now .

383
00:24:04,133 --> 00:24:07,409
They 're standing on an eight-foot platform . No , it 's not right on the edge .

384
00:24:07,493 --> 00:24:09,051
It 's about eight feet from the edge .

385
00:24:09,133 --> 00:24:11,203
But the fact is that they 're standing there .

386
00:24:11,293 --> 00:24:14,524
We had to get this whole thing in one day , and they have to do

387
00:24:14,613 --> 00:24:19,164
a very personal scene while they 're perched on the top of this building .

388
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:25,332
You can see Al , at that moment , trying to let us know a little bit how precarious it is .

389
00:24:25,413 --> 00:24:30,168
But do you notice any kind of nervousness from Pacino ? Not at all . He 's easy .

390
00:24:30,493 --> 00:24:34,008
And the whole essence here is that Keanu 's sitting out there . One , his mind is blown

391
00:24:34,093 --> 00:24:36,732
at the beginning , and then somehow he finds himself getting into it .

392
00:24:36,813 --> 00:24:38,690
And at the same time , he looks right here and says :

393
00:24:38,773 --> 00:24:43,085
" My God , John Milton 's standing like a foot from the edge of a 50-story precipice .

394
00:24:43,173 --> 00:24:44,526
" What kind of guy is this ? "

395
00:24:44,613 --> 00:24:47,605
He also wears elevator shoes , which I think is interesting .

396
00:24:47,693 --> 00:24:51,163
But the fact is , right here is what the film also is about .

397
00:24:51,253 --> 00:24:53,767
It 's about pressure . It 's about professionalism .

398
00:24:53,853 --> 00:24:57,289
And what John Milton has done is taken Keanu Reeves

399
00:24:57,413 --> 00:25:00,769
or Kevin Lomax , in this case , up to the precipice .

400
00:25:01,013 --> 00:25:03,288
He 's showing him : " All this can be yours . "

401
00:25:03,373 --> 00:25:08,049
And what is it ? It 's Wall Street . It 's the seat of capitalistic power in the world .

402
00:25:08,133 --> 00:25:11,170
And he 's basically saying , you know , I know you 're a hotshot

403
00:25:11,253 --> 00:25:13,642
but can you take the pressure ? Can you sleep at night ?

404
00:25:13,933 --> 00:25:19,132
That little speech that Tony Gilroy wrote , I think , fits all professionals in this instance .

405
00:25:19,213 --> 00:25:23,047
When you have to deliver on a deadline , you know what he 's talking about .

406
00:25:23,133 --> 00:25:26,364
Basically , Kevin is there . He 's ready . He said , " What about money ? "

407
00:25:26,453 --> 00:25:29,331
Milton laughs . " Money ? That 's the easy part . "

408
00:25:29,493 --> 00:25:31,723
Kevin doesn 't have any problem . He can sleep at night . He 's a lawyer .

409
00:25:31,813 --> 00:25:33,451
He knows how to do it .

410
00:25:33,533 --> 00:25:38,607
We cut from that to Carnegie Hill , which is Fifth Avenue in the Nineties in New York .

411
00:25:38,893 --> 00:25:43,887
It 's probably the most exclusive address in New York . Central Park is on one side .

412
00:25:44,013 --> 00:25:48,643
You have these beautiful , beautiful buildings with fantastic apartments inside .

413
00:25:48,733 --> 00:25:51,452
And the Heaths . You 're meeting Jackie Heath for the first time .

414
00:25:51,533 --> 00:25:55,845
I reveal her with that wipe from the elevator , you see her in close-up .

415
00:25:57,053 --> 00:26:00,966
Leamon Heath and Jackie Heath , they are absolutely New Yorkers .

416
00:26:02,333 --> 00:26:06,884
They 've maintained their integrity as black people , but at the same time

417
00:26:07,093 --> 00:26:11,644
they are not about to resist the temptations of the city . They want it .

418
00:26:12,653 --> 00:26:15,406
They know how to deal with it . They 're very sophisticated .

419
00:26:15,493 --> 00:26:18,053
Look at the clothes that Jackie 's wearing .

420
00:26:18,133 --> 00:26:20,010
Leamon makes the money and she knows how to spend it

421
00:26:20,093 --> 00:26:22,243
and she doesn 't have any qualms about it .

422
00:26:22,333 --> 00:26:26,326
This apartment , I wanted to basically establish the sense of awe .

423
00:26:28,213 --> 00:26:32,491
You know , John Milton owns this building . He has it for his employees .

424
00:26:33,213 --> 00:26:37,172
Although it 's usually for partners , and for Kevin Lomax to get an apartment first up

425
00:26:37,253 --> 00:26:40,643
shows that he 's a little special , and you can feel , right here

426
00:26:40,733 --> 00:26:43,122
that they 're a little jealous .

427
00:26:43,213 --> 00:26:44,771
" Took us six years to get in here . "

428
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:47,162
Every New Yorker will understand that when they really want to get into

429
00:26:47,253 --> 00:26:50,131
a big building . This is a film about New York .

430
00:26:50,213 --> 00:26:53,967
Tony Gilroy , who lives in New York and understands it incredibly well

431
00:26:54,053 --> 00:26:57,602
is able to put these nuances in here that are maybe not aimed at everyone .

432
00:26:57,693 --> 00:26:59,445
But certainly , you know , you make a film in New York

433
00:26:59,533 --> 00:27:02,889
it was important to me that you do something real .

434
00:27:03,573 --> 00:27:07,088
Now , you know , Kevin has basically been offered the job .

435
00:27:07,173 --> 00:27:10,927
He 's got to now sell his wife on it . And this is a big test .

436
00:27:11,653 --> 00:27:14,565
If she , you know ... He says , " I 'll take you home if you want . "

437
00:27:14,653 --> 00:27:17,406
Of course , if she did , God knows what he 'd think .

438
00:27:17,493 --> 00:27:19,484
She knows him . She knows what he wants .

439
00:27:19,573 --> 00:27:21,450
And at the same time , how could you turn this down ?

440
00:27:21,533 --> 00:27:23,808
It 's very important right now , at this moment

441
00:27:23,893 --> 00:27:27,886
to understand that Mary Ann wants this as badly as Kevin does .

442
00:27:28,053 --> 00:27:32,285
I mean , who would resist ? Come on . They 're too big for a small pond .

443
00:27:32,373 --> 00:27:35,809
