I actually gave him his first big break in films on Everybody 's All American .

1779
01:50:26,415 --> 01:50:31,409
We got back together on this film , and he has repaid me immeasurably on this score .

1780
01:50:32,215 --> 01:50:35,730
I think he created a brilliant score for this film . There 's a lot of music .

1781
01:50:35,815 --> 01:50:40,843
It 's a very difficult piece to do . The music has to be the emotional core of the piece .

1782
01:50:40,935 --> 01:50:43,813
It has to establish how everyone is feeling .

1783
01:50:43,895 --> 01:50:47,854
And I think there are moments of grandeur , of huge , huge cues

1784
01:50:49,295 --> 01:50:53,083
and , at the same time , there are many very quiet , very sad moments .

1785
01:50:54,215 --> 01:50:57,890
And I think the music that 's happening in this scene actually complements it

1786
01:50:57,975 --> 01:51:00,284
