01:53:18,135 --> 01:53:20,012
He 's got to be charming . He 's got to be sexy .

1825
01:53:20,095 --> 01:53:22,450
He 's got to be smart . He 's got to be totally seductive .

1826
01:53:22,535 --> 01:53:27,086
But ultimately , he 's got to be evil . And Al has the courage to go after it .

1827
01:53:28,135 --> 01:53:31,650
I mean , the great thing about Al Pacino is that he will risk artistic suicide

1828
01:53:31,735 --> 01:53:34,693
in every single film he tries . Too many ...

1829
01:53:35,095 --> 01:53:38,565
I mean , how many Hollywood stars settle ? They 're smart .

1830
01:53:39,215 --> 01:53:40,773
You know , " Why should I change ?

1831
01:53:40,855 --> 01:53:43,050
" They 're paying me all this money to be just the same . "

1832
01:53:43,135 --> 01:53:46,445
Pacino won 't do that . He goes after it . He risks everything .

1833
01:53:46,535 --> 01:53:48,412
And some people don 't like him for it .

1834
01:53:48,495 --> 01:53:51,009
But who could do this scene , but Al Pacino ?

1835
01:53:51,095 --> 01:53:54,405
This is a dense scene . Tony Gilroy wrote this scene .

1836
01:53:55,095 --> 01:53:57,484
It 's full of words . It 's almost a monologue .

1837
01:53:57,575 --> 01:54:01,170
It is not supposed to be realistic . It 's not supposed to be mumbly

1838
01:54:01,255 --> 01:54:05,453
you know , the new word of Hollywood , realistic acting , real mumbly .

1839
01:54:05,535 --> 01:54:09,494
No , this guy 's articulate . He is bigger than life . He has a lot to say .

1840
01:54:09,575 --> 01:54:13,568
He 's lived forever and he is confronting us and he 's confronting Kevin

1841
01:54:13,655 --> 01:54:17,091
with the realities of the fact that he 's the devil .

1842
01:54:18,415 --> 01:54:21,168
He exists and he 's been there all along .

1843
01:54:21,855 --> 01:54:24,653
And as Kevin initially begins with this

1844
01:54:24,735 --> 01:54:28,171
