1852
01:54:57,455 --> 01:54:59,730
And the devil will . The devil 's gonna be funny .

1853
01:54:59,815 --> 01:55:01,965
He 's gonna be charming . He 's gonna be witty .

1854
01:55:02,055 --> 01:55:05,650
And in this scene , it was a tour de force opportunity for Al Pacino

1855
01:55:05,735 --> 01:55:09,489
to show some things that he hasn 't shown before , I think .

1856
01:55:21,095 --> 01:55:25,407
We rehearsed this scene for about a week . It was the one , I must say

1857
01:55:26,215 --> 01:55:28,092
for Warner Bros. , a great thing they did for me .

1858
01:55:28,175 --> 01:55:31,008
And although we had our differences , I was able to get my vision on the screen .

1859
01:55:31,095 --> 01:55:33,563
I have no excuses . So , I do thank them .

1860
01:55:33,655 --> 01:55:36,692
There was a great thing here in that Warner Bros. Allowed us

1861
01:55:36,775 --> 01:55:39,335
to come back from New York . We built this set in Los Angeles .

1862
01:55:39,415 --> 01:55:44,091
I had a week to prepare the set , to light it and to rehearse with the actors .

1863
01:55:44,895 --> 01:55:48,331
Al , Keanu and Connie and myself , worked there alone

1864
01:55:49,455 --> 01:55:54,165
and really kind of built this scene . Tony Gilroy was there also , pardon me .

1865
01:55:54,535 --> 01:55:59,051
It is not an easy scene to do when you realize it 's basically a monologue .

1866
01:55:59,415 --> 01:56:02,327
How do you keep it moving ? How do you keep it visual ?

1867
01:56:02,415 --> 01:56:06,044
And it 's basically a confrontation . And again , as I said

1868
01:56:06,175 --> 01:56:08,894
I want the devil to be confronting us .

1869
01:56:09,055 --> 01:56:12,934
We all take credit for the things that we do in life that are good .

1870
01:56:13,015 --> 01:56:16,405
When it 's a good decision , " I made that decision . I 'll take credit for that . "

1871
