1885
01:57:08,415 --> 01:57:12,010
and I think are the most pragmatic of all professions .

1886
01:57:12,895 --> 01:57:17,047
However , all professionals find themselves in a position to blame

1887
01:57:17,455 --> 01:57:22,085
or be able to use their corporate entity , their boss , their organization

1888
01:57:22,175 --> 01:57:26,134
their professional oath as a screen against having to confront

1889
01:57:26,215 --> 01:57:28,809
moral realities , personal choices .

1890
01:57:29,175 --> 01:57:33,453
If you can say " My personal , professional oath , " pardon me , not my ...

1891
01:57:34,135 --> 01:57:37,445
" My professional oath says that I 'm absolved from responsibility ...

1892
01:57:37,535 --> 01:57:41,005
" ... because I have to represent my client to the best of my ability . "

1893
01:57:41,095 --> 01:57:45,691
Or , " My corporation says I need to do this , pollute this lake , and I 'm doing it . "

1894
01:57:45,775 --> 01:57:49,245
It absolves you of your personal , moral responsibility .

1895
01:57:49,495 --> 01:57:53,613
What this whole scene is about is confronting your own hypocrisy

1896
01:57:53,775 --> 01:57:57,450
and saying your ambition , your own vanity , in a world that 's fiber-optically

1897
01:57:57,535 --> 01:58:02,245
interconnected to satisfy our every eager impulse , " You , " meaning , " You humans "

1898
01:58:02,335 --> 01:58:04,610
as Milton says , " are exactly ...

1899
01:58:05,015 --> 01:58:09,691
" I 've succeeded beyond my wildest dreams just by letting you do what you want .

1900
01:58:10,055 --> 01:58:12,523
" You 're so selfish . You 're so self-involved . "

1901
01:58:12,615 --> 01:58:15,083
So that 's what this scene is about .

1902
01:58:15,335 --> 01:58:17,326
Kevin realizes that it 's true

1903
