because Al Pacino is basically talking about his father .

1918
01:59:14,775 --> 01:59:18,404
He 's talking about his former boss . He 's his own boss now .

1919
01:59:19,615 --> 01:59:22,732
But if you think of Lucifer , the fallen angel

1920
01:59:25,215 --> 01:59:28,093
the brightest , the most honored and the most

1921
01:59:28,175 --> 01:59:30,052
you know , he was God 's favorite

1922
01:59:30,135 --> 01:59:34,174
being thrown out of heaven because of ego , because he didn 't want to take orders .

1923
01:59:34,255 --> 01:59:36,564
That 's what Pacino 's doing here .

1924
01:59:38,615 --> 01:59:41,254
Look . He 's angry . He 's losing control .

1925
01:59:46,495 --> 01:59:49,646
He 's a child having a tantrum against a father

1926
01:59:50,055 --> 01:59:53,650
who he could never quite get the best of and he still resents .

1927
01:59:53,735 --> 01:59:56,044
He 's still angry that he got thrown out of heaven .

1928
01:59:56,135 --> 01:59:58,695
He made the choice to be down here on the Earth .

1929
01:59:58,775 --> 02:00:00,686
He 's been here since the whole thing began .

1930
02:00:00,775 --> 02:00:03,448
He 's had his nose in . He 's encouraged man .

1931
02:00:03,535 --> 02:00:05,526
He 's taken the opposite course .

1932
02:00:05,615 --> 02:00:09,005
But in this scene , what he 's basically doing is drawing the line .

1933
02:00:09,095 --> 02:00:13,930
He 's telling Kevin , " This is my world down here , human beings . And I love them .

1934
02:00:16,375 --> 02:00:19,287
" Which way do you want to go ? Who are you gonna choose ? "

1935
02:00:19,375 --> 02:00:22,606
And I think the idea of " I 'm a humanist , the last humanist ... "

1936
02:00:22,695 --> 02:00:25,129
... there are very funny things here .

1937
02:00:25,215 --> 02:00:28,287
" Who , in their possible mind , who in their right mind could possibly deny ...

1938
02:00:28,375 --> 02:00:30,013
" ... that the 20th century was entirely mine ? "

1939
02:00:30,095 --> 02:00:33,804
When you see this film in a theater , the audience has a big laugh at that point

1940
02:00:33,895 --> 02:00:38,173
because you have to admit there 's been a lot of evil in the world in the 20th century

1941
02:00:38,255 --> 02:00:40,325
and at this point he 's saying , " It 's my time .

1942
02:00:40,415 --> 02:00:43,452
" I 'm on the verge of the next millennium and the rest of it 's gonna be mine .

1943
02:00:43,535 --> 02:00:44,331
" Come and join me . "

1944
02:00:45,295 --> 02:00:50,130
I think that what we were trying to do here , in this scene , is deal with a lot of

1945
02:00:50,215 --> 02:00:52,285
philosophical elements , trying to make a film

1946
02:00:52,375 --> 02:00:55,094
trying to make a devil that we deserve today .

1947
02:00:55,175 --> 02:00:59,771
You know , this is an age-old story , a Faustian tale , and what Tony Gilroy

1948
02:00:59,855 --> 02:01:03,643
and I wanted to do , and Al , was try to create something

1949
02:01:04,455 --> 02:01:06,969
that you may not have seen before .

1950
02:01:07,055 --> 02:01:11,333
And it ultimately builds to something . Kevin is a lawyer . He 's smart .

1951
02:01:11,855 --> 02:01:14,847
After having been so emotional and falling apart

1952
02:01:14,935 --> 02:01:18,132
he starts to kind of reason , " Why ? What are you really after ? "

1953
02:01:18,215 --> 02:01:20,809
And the thing that we 're trying to build here is something

1954
02:01:20,895 --> 02:01:22,965
that you may not have seen in another film .

1955
02:01:23,055 --> 02:01:27,207
Here is an instance in which , " You 're going to mate with your sister ...

1956
02:01:27,295 --> 02:01:29,092
" ... and create the Antichrist . "

1957
02:01:29,175 --> 02:01:32,087
Kevin , who up to this point , you think it 's for his soul .

1958
02:01:32,175 --> 02:01:35,406
No , it 's not just for his soul . It 's something to create

